implementationPlan.description:
Implement the precedence and the command rewrite (DoD 1 and 2) in moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/services/MoeDaemonSupervisor.kt with the session's own editing tool (Edit on a Claude seat, apply_patch on a codex exec seat), never a shell write or a subagent. Keep every hunk in the four places below: sibling task-fe811130 (bindHost probe, not yet planned) edits isReachable, the :151-166 reuse/delete block, DaemonInfo and this file's companion object.

(a) Constructor seam, inserted directly after the `processLookup` parameter (:43), before `replaceConfirmer`:
    // MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND, injected by tests because a JVM cannot change its own environment.
    private val daemonCommandOverride: () -> String? = { System.getenv("MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND") },
Not earlier: RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt:2243 passes the first 11 parameters (through processLookup) positionally, so an insertion before position 12 breaks its compile. Not after docSync: a seam fe811130 may append there would collide in the merge.

(b) Spawn selection in ensureDaemonRunningImpl (:182). Replace
    val direct = if (isProtected) protectedCommandOrRefuse(projectBasePath) ?: return false else buildDirectDaemonCommand(projectBasePath)
with
    // A set MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND wins over every daemon script; the protected profile never reads the environment.
    val overrideCommand = if (isProtected) null else daemonCommandOverrideOrNull()
    val direct = when {
        isProtected -> protectedCommandOrRefuse(projectBasePath) ?: return false
        overrideCommand != null -> null
        else -> buildDirectDaemonCommand(projectBasePath)
    }
and at :190 pass it on: `val command = buildDaemonCommand(projectBasePath, overrideCommand)`. One read per call, so the selection and the command always agree.

(c) Replace buildDaemonCommand (:665-691). The installed start-daemon.cmd branch and the `moe-daemon start` fallback stay as they are; only the override branch changes, and hostSuffix moves to the top:
    internal fun buildDaemonCommand(basePath: String, overrideCommand: String? = daemonCommandOverrideOrNull()): String {
        val hostSuffix = if (wslAgentsEnabled()) " --host $WSL_BIND_HOST" else ""
        val raw = overrideCommand?.trim()?.takeIf { it.isNotEmpty() }
        if (raw != null) {
            val words = commandWords(raw)
            val command = when {
                raw.contains("{projectPath}") -> raw.replace("{projectPath}", basePath)
                raw.contains("--project") -> raw
                words.drop(1).any { it in daemonSubcommands } -> "$raw --project \"$basePath\""
                else -> "$raw start --project \"$basePath\""
            }
            return if ("--host" in words) command else command + hostSuffix
        }
        // the installed branch and the fallback, unchanged
    }
KDoc it with the rules: {projectPath} is substituted, and a command carrying it or --project is otherwise used as written; any other command gets `start` unless a word after the first is a daemon subcommand, then `--project "<basePath>"`; WSL agent mode appends ` --host wsl` unless a word of the command is `--host`. Why `start` is only appended: the daemon reads its subcommand only as its first argument (packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts parseArgs, `args[0] || 'start'`), so nothing appended fixes a command with arguments of its own, and CONFIGURATION.md tells the operator to name it. The DoD's "leaves unchanged a command that already names a subcommand" means no `start` is inserted; `--project` is still appended exactly as today.

(d) Directly after buildDaemonCommand (not in the companion object) add:
    private fun daemonCommandOverrideOrNull(): String? = try {
        daemonCommandOverride()?.trim()?.takeIf { it.isNotEmpty() }
    } catch (ex: Exception) {
        log.warn("Cannot read MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND; starting the daemon without it", ex)
        null
    }
    // The daemon CLI's subcommands: the word cases of main() in packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts, plus accounts.
    private val daemonSubcommands = setOf("start", "stop", "status", "init", "doctor", "version", "accounts", "check-architecture", "_run")
    /** The command's words as a shell splits them, quotes removed: a quoted path with spaces is one word. */
    private fun commandWords(command: String): List<String> =
        Regex("\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*'|\\S+").findAll(command).map { it.value.trim('"', '\'') }.toList()
-v and --version are left out: they are flags, not subcommands.

Error handling: a seam that throws (a SecurityException reading the environment) is logged and treated as unset, so the bundled daemon still starts; spawn failures stay in the existing try/catch that publishes onStatus(false, ...). The protected branch never calls daemonCommandOverride (test O2 pins it).

TESTS (DoD 1 and 2). Create moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/services/MoeDaemonCommandOverrideTest.kt (JUnit 4 with a TemporaryFolder rule, like its neighbours) with the session's own editing tool. It is a class of its own so that task-fe811130's cases in MoeDaemonSupervisorTest.kt never meet these in a merge. MoeDaemonSupervisorTest.FakeProcess is private, so add a private nested `StubProcess : Process()`: alive until destroy() or waitFor(), empty input and error streams, a ByteArrayOutputStream output, and exitValue() throwing IllegalThreadStateException while alive. Expectations are literal strings with the literal "wsl", never the production constant or helpers. The spawn prefix is `if (MoeDaemonSupervisor.isWindowsHost()) listOf("cmd", "/c") else listOf("bash", "-lc")`, because the gate runs on Windows. Every supervisor gets profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY } (O2 excepted) and docSync = { _, _ -> }. Below, p is /srv/my proj, Q is p wrapped in double quotes, and R is root.absolutePath wrapped in double quotes.

O1 `O1 a set override wins over a resolving daemon script and an unset or blank one keeps the direct spawn`. root is a new folder holding .moe/ and a written packages/moe-daemon/dist/index.js (the script findInParents resolves, as in W1). A helper spawn(wsl, seam) builds a supervisor with processStarter = { started += it.command().toList(); StubProcess() }, wslAgentsEnabled = { wsl } and daemonCommandOverride = seam, asserts that ensureDaemonRunning() is true and returns started.single(). Pins:
- { "npx moe-daemon" } gives the prefix + `npx moe-daemon start --project R`;
- the same with wsl = true gives the prefix + `npx moe-daemon start --project R --host wsl`;
- { null }, { "" }, { "   " } and { throw SecurityException("denied") } each give cmd.drop(2) == listOf("start", "--project", root.absolutePath) and File(cmd[1]).canonicalFile == script.canonicalFile: today's direct spawn. The throw covers the error handling: unreadable counts as unset.
O2 `O2 the protected profile never reads the override`: profile = { RuntimeProfile.PROTECTED }, installedRoot = { null }, nodeExecutable = { null }, daemonCommandOverride = { reads++; "npx moe-daemon" } and a recording processStarter. ensureDaemonRunning() is false, reads == 0 and nothing started (installedArtifact(null, ...) refuses with "installed Moe runtime not found").
O3 `O3 a command naming no daemon subcommand gets start and one naming a subcommand keeps its own` (wsl false; supervisor.buildDaemonCommand(p, raw); exact equality):
- `npx moe-daemon` -> `npx moe-daemon start --project Q` (the documented example);
- `moe-daemon` -> `moe-daemon start --project Q`;
- `node /opt/moe/daemon/index.js` -> `node /opt/moe/daemon/index.js start --project Q`;
- the installer's value, C:\Program Files\Moe\moe-daemon\start-daemon.cmd wrapped in double quotes -> that value + ` start --project Q`;
- `node "/opt/my start/index.js"` -> that value + ` start --project Q` (a quoted word is not a subcommand);
- `npx moe-daemon start` -> `npx moe-daemon start --project Q` (no second start);
- `npx moe-daemon init` -> `npx moe-daemon init --project Q`;
- `  npx moe-daemon  ` -> `npx moe-daemon start --project Q` (trimmed);
- buildDaemonCommand(p, "   ") == buildDaemonCommand(p, null): blank is unset. Compare the two, because the unset branch may find a real installed start-daemon.cmd on a Windows host.
No result above contains "--host".
O4 `O4 a command carrying --project or {projectPath} is used as written` (wsl false):
- `node /opt/moe/index.js start --project "{projectPath}"` -> `node /opt/moe/index.js start --project Q`;
- `my-wrapper {projectPath}` -> `my-wrapper /srv/my proj`;
- `npx moe-daemon start --project /srv/other` -> unchanged;
- `npx moe-daemon --project /srv/other` -> unchanged. Comment it: the daemon reads its subcommand only as its first argument, so an appended start could not fix it, and CONFIGURATION.md tells the operator to name it.
O5 `O5 WSL agent mode appends --host wsl unless the command carries --host` (wsl true):
- `npx moe-daemon` -> `npx moe-daemon start --project Q --host wsl`;
- `npx moe-daemon start --host 127.0.0.1` -> `npx moe-daemon start --host 127.0.0.1 --project Q` (exactly one --host);
- `node /opt/moe/index.js start --project "{projectPath}"` -> `node /opt/moe/index.js start --project Q --host wsl`;
- `npx moe-daemon start --project /srv/other` -> `npx moe-daemon start --project /srv/other --host wsl`.

Then in MoeDaemonSupervisorTest.kt touch only W1 and W2 (:503-543), so that the new precedence cannot flip them on a machine whose environment sets MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND (the Windows installer sets it):
- W1's constructor call gains `daemonCommandOverride = { null }`;
- in W2, delete the stale comment line `// MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND is the operator's verbatim command and never carries --host.` and the `Assume.assumeTrue(System.getenv("MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND").isNullOrBlank())` line, and add `daemonCommandOverride = { null }` to its constructor call.
Keep the Assume import, which other tests use. Add nothing else to that file: task-fe811130 adds its cases there.

SELF-REVIEW once, as the last step (load adversarial-self-review), over this task's diff only. The plan was written without a Gradle dry run, so prove the tests bite with mutants in an archive copy, never in the worktree (mem:gotcha-jetbrains-qa-mutants-in-archive-copy, Worker variant): `git archive HEAD moe-jetbrains | tar -x -C /mnt/d/moe-scratch/m8383/repo`, copy this task's changed and new files over it, then for each mutant make one exact-anchor replace, run `cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\moe-scratch\m8383\repo\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --tests com.moe.services.MoeDaemonCommandOverrideTest --rerun"` under the lease, restore, and check the sha256. Each must turn red:
- M1: the selection keeps buildDirectDaemonCommand when an override is set (O1);
- M2: the `overrideCommand != null` branch moved before `isProtected`, with the read made unconditional (O2);
- M3: the old extension rule, `start` only for .cmd/.ps1/.js or `moe-daemon` (O3);
- M4: commandWords as a plain whitespace split (O3, the quoted path);
- M5: the override branch drops hostSuffix (O5).
Name each mutant's failing test in the complete_task summary. Then the checklist:
- two ensureDaemonRunning calls racing: one override read per call, cooldown and attempt counters unchanged;
- null, blank, padded, quoted and huge values;
- a value carrying both {projectPath} and --host;
- the Windows `cmd /c` and POSIX `bash -lc` prefixes;
- nothing under PROTECTED calls daemonCommandOverride;
- MoeDaemonSupervisorTest.kt changed only in W1 and W2;
- `git diff --stat` shows exactly the four planned files.
If the review changes any byte, re-run step 4's command and use that output as the evidence.
